WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:01.401
Just a moment ago.

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:01.701
As the

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:02.135
White House

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.670
now says the President Biden

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:04.170
is going

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.305
to leave a dinner

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:07.941
with fellow G7 leaders early

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:09.542
because he's going back to his hotel

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.378
to get an update from his team

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:13.346
on the debt limit negotiations.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:14.781
The crisis back in Washington

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:16.516
has been overshadowing Biden's

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:17.851
crucial foreign trip

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.085
during a critical moment.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.121
And Russia's invasion of Ukraine.

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:21.788
We're now learning

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.123
also this morning that Ukrainian

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:24.357
President Zelensky

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.658
is also going to Japan

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:27.727
to meet face to face with President Biden

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.763
and the other G7 leaders

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:30.930
Sources tell CNN he's

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.766
going to arrive Saturday evening

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:34.567
and meet with them on Sunday.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:35.468
Just this morning,

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.470
the G7 leaders put out a statement

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.039
vowing to support Russia,

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:39.773
vowing to support

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:41.775
Ukraine against Russia's brutal invasion

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.943
for, quote, as long as it takes.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.545
And we're told a big topic of discussion

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:45.812
will be

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:46.279
whether or not

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:47.447
to send those F-16

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:48.181
fighter jets

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:49.616
to Ukraine's Air Force

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:50.583
to potentially help them

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:52.385
turn the tide in this war.

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:53.286
Sources say the U.S.

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:55.321
is now signaling it will not block U.S.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:57.190
allies from exporting them.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:59.092
So Lenski has been on a whirlwind

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:01.094
of diplomatic missions across Europe.

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:02.762
He just arrived in Saudi Arabia

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:03.997
to meet with the Arab League.

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:05.532
He has been pushing allies

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:07.400
to send more weapons as his troops

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.702
prepare for a crucial counteroffensive.

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:11.071
One of his biggest demands

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:13.173
has been those F-16 fighter jets.

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:14.441
Nic Robertson is live on the ground

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:15.241
in eastern Ukraine,

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.443
not far from the front lines.

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:18.011
Nick, glad to have you with us.

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:18.545
His trip

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:20.046
the fact that he's going in-person, he's

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:21.781
not joining them remotely.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:22.749
He's going

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.217
because he thinks it's crucial

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:26.252
to be face to face with President Biden

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:28.054
for F-16s.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.255
I'm sure but also with these

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.390
other European leaders

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.727
Yeah, we know the F-16s are going to be,

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.896
you know, top of the agenda for Zelensky

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.598
because it has been for some time.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:39.132
He knows he's

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:40.366
beginning to win the argument

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:41.000
that he's won over

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.268
some of these European leaders.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:43.403
He was meeting with them

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:45.238
in their capitals earlier in the week.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:46.606
Those leaders met in Iceland

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:47.640
a couple of days ago,

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.410
and they came up with a plan to help

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:51.778
get Ukrainian fighter

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:52.579
pilots trained

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:53.413
for the F-16

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:54.347
to help the Ukrainians

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.483
figure out how to purchase F-16s.

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:57.784
Zelensky's,

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:58.918
advisers are saying

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:00.420
it's extremely important

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:00.820
for him

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.422
to be there in person

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:06.493
to explain their thinking, to put forward

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:07.594
their proposals,

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:09.529
to put forward their arguments

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.131
and really give the leaders

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:11.531
the best

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:13.266
the most accurate, up to date sense

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:14.200
of what's happening

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.969
in the war here in Ukraine.

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.170
And for Zelensky,

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:18.138
that that is

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:19.772
quite simply going to come out

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:22.075
with the need to push for more ammunition

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:24.010
and the need to get those fighter jets.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.146
And he thinks best way to get this

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:27.180
done for him,

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.448
be there in person,

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:30.483
make the case face to face.

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.252
Yeah. It's a powerful argument to make.

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.119
But before he gets to

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:35.054
Japan, he's just landed in

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:36.623
Jeddah in Saudi Arabia, Nick.

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:37.423
And obviously

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:39.292
there are some very wealthy

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:40.059
Gulf state leaders

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:40.927
there that have provided

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:42.595
a substantial amount

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:44.063
of assistance to Ukraine.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.765
What's the expectation for this

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:48.434
stop before he gets to that G7 meeting?

00:02:50.904 --> 00:02:51.304
Yes, he's

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:51.804
slated to

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.606
have a bilateral with

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:55.642
Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman,

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:58.111
the crown prince of Saudi, perhaps

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.612
not well-liked on on

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.514
some aspects on the world stage,

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:03.283
but he has been hugely busy

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:04.284
behind the scenes

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:05.485
trying to help with things

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:06.886
like prisoner releases,

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:07.954
prisoner exchanges.

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:10.089
And this will be a topic of conversation

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:10.790
for Zelensky.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.859
But he'll also talk about the Muslims

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:15.762
in Ukraine, the Crimean Tatars

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:16.696
who are facing

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:18.698
political oppression in Crimea

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:19.699
under the Russians

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:21.668
That will be a topic of discussion.

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:23.102
But what Zelensky

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:25.538
recognizes is and his fault and

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.208
sorry, that's up

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:29.609
and ready to speak with morning

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:31.177
just being cleared here

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.912
they come in quite often.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.981
What Zelensky will be talking about

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.549
will be the plight of the Tatars

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.284
in Crimea under Russian rule,

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:40.286
but also he recognizes

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:41.888
that the crown prince, Mohammed bin

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.690
Salman, wants to play a role

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:44.857
in stabilizing

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.893
and a potential peace deal down the road.

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.962
So that will be part of the conversation.

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:49.562
There as well.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.598
The foreign minister of Saudi was in

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:53.766
Kiev a couple of months ago

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:54.901
talking about support

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.169
that the country can give.

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:59.072
Zelensky understands as well the members

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.707
as a relationship with Putin

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:03.109
can get in Putin's mindset.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:03.743
There's a lot on

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.011
there's a lot that Zelensky

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:06.112
can get out of this meeting.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:08.915
Nick, thank you for being

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.783
there for us on both those fronts.

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.952
CNN's Jomana Karadsheh joins us now

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:14.921
from Istanbul to discuss. Jomana.

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:15.688
What struck you

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:16.689
about what we've just heard

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:18.558
from the president's events

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:22.862
Well, it's very interesting

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:25.498
beyond quite a pretty bold move by

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:26.799
the Ukrainian president

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:28.701
to show up in a region

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:30.169
that has, for the most part,

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:34.440
tried to stay out of the Ukrainian war.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.441
That has really tried

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:36.809
to stay on the fence.

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.278
This is a region

00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:40.046
where you have countries with very close

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:41.514
ties as well

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:44.550
to Russia, economic and military ties.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.586
And he's really trying to reach out

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:47.420
to these countries.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:48.321
Of course,

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:48.855
you know,

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:49.656
with all the talk

00:04:49.656 --> 00:04:51.924
about the spring offensive in the works

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:53.159
right now.

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:54.794
It does appear that he is trying

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:56.095
to reach out to these countries

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:58.998
that have really tried to stay out of it.

00:04:58.998 --> 00:04:59.632
For the most part

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:01.501
with Saudi Arabia, for example,

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.069
they have really tried to emerge

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:04.537
as a mediator

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:06.439
in this region, whether it is

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:08.508
brokering a

00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:09.575
prisoner swap

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:11.311
deal a few months ago

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:13.513
between Ukraine and Russia

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:15.248
or whether it is

00:05:15.248 --> 00:05:16.849
other conflicts in this region.

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:17.317
So you see

00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:18.618
President Zelensky really

00:05:18.618 --> 00:05:20.687
trying to reach out to them,

00:05:20.687 --> 00:05:22.188
talking about

00:05:22.188 --> 00:05:25.858
Muslim Ukrainians who are victims of the

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:28.895
of the oppression in the aggression

00:05:28.895 --> 00:05:31.431
and really trying to speak to this

00:05:31.431 --> 00:05:33.766
region, giving them examples of,

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.002
you know, what Ukrainians

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:36.903
are going through,

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:38.271
saying that

00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:41.240
you would not accept foreigners

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:43.476
taking away your children, foreigners

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:44.610
taking your land,

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.946
invading your country, really trying

00:05:47.814 --> 00:05:50.149
to to to connect

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:51.384
with this region

00:05:51.384 --> 00:05:53.453
that is economically important.

00:05:54.253 --> 00:05:55.955
And of course, a very,

00:05:55.955 --> 00:05:58.891
very interesting time to also be

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:00.426
at this summit, Bianca,

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:01.694
and doing this at a time

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:03.129
where all eyes were already

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:04.931
on this Arab League

00:06:04.931 --> 00:06:08.000
leaders meeting because Bashar al-Assad,

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:09.902
the Syrian president,

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:12.939
who for more than a decade now

00:06:12.939 --> 00:06:13.873
has been a pariah

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:15.041
on the international stage,

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:15.742
has been

00:06:15.742 --> 00:06:16.743
brought back

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:18.778
into the regional and Arab fold.

00:06:18.778 --> 00:06:21.280
He was making his appearance today

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:21.881
at this summit.

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:23.983
We have seen him shaking hands with the

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:25.918
with the

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:26.753
Saudi crown

00:06:26.753 --> 00:06:27.487
Prince Mohammed

00:06:27.487 --> 00:06:30.289
bin Salman, all smiles being welcomed

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:32.892
with handshakes and red carpets

00:06:32.892 --> 00:06:34.260
to this summit.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.328
So all eyes were on that.

00:06:35.328 --> 00:06:36.729
And it's going to be very interesting

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:38.364
to see

00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:40.633
both President Zelensky

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:42.802
and Bashar al-Assad at this summit,

00:06:42.802 --> 00:06:45.972
which we haven't actually seen just yet.

00:06:47.106 --> 00:06:49.275
Because, you know, over the past year

00:06:49.275 --> 00:06:50.309
or so, Bianca,

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:52.412
I've been speaking to a lot of Syrians

00:06:52.412 --> 00:06:55.081
who see a lot of parallels between what

00:06:55.081 --> 00:06:56.182
they have gone

00:06:56.182 --> 00:06:57.550
through over the past decade.

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:59.619
Of course, because Russia backed

00:06:59.886 --> 00:07:00.853
President Assad,

00:07:00.853 --> 00:07:02.955
it is the reason he survived

00:07:02.955 --> 00:07:04.557
the civil war in his country.

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:06.559
It is the reason why he has

00:07:06.559 --> 00:07:07.493
emerged

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:09.796
pretty much victorious in this war.

00:07:09.796 --> 00:07:11.197
And so many Syrians feel

00:07:11.197 --> 00:07:13.800
that they are the victims of that

00:07:14.534 --> 00:07:17.303
Russian support for President Assad.

00:07:17.303 --> 00:07:18.337
And they have always drawn

00:07:18.337 --> 00:07:19.238
these similarities

00:07:19.238 --> 00:07:21.274
between Russia and Ukraine, saying

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:24.777
if the world had stopped Syria, Russia

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:26.746
in Syria,

00:07:26.746 --> 00:07:27.647
they believe Ukraine

00:07:27.647 --> 00:07:28.514
wouldn't have happened.

00:07:29.715 --> 00:07:30.750
It is fascinating to

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:33.986
see that clash of geopolitical alignment

00:07:34.487 --> 00:07:35.421
really coming to the fore

00:07:35.421 --> 00:07:36.122
at this summit

00:07:36.122 --> 00:07:37.190
and the Arab League

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:38.558
deciding that engagement

00:07:38.558 --> 00:07:40.393
is the way forward with Bashar al-Assad,

00:07:40.393 --> 00:07:41.861
unlike most Western countries.

00:07:41.861 --> 00:07:42.562
Jomana Karadsheh

00:07:42.562 --> 00:07:45.331
live in Istanbul, thank you so much.

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:47.266
Following his stop in Saudi Arabia,

00:07:47.266 --> 00:07:48.801
officials say that President Zelensky

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:49.402
is expected

00:07:49.402 --> 00:07:51.504
to head to Japan for an in-person

00:07:51.504 --> 00:07:53.372
visit to the G7 summit.

00:07:53.372 --> 00:07:54.440
It comes as G7

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:55.675
leaders were set to discuss

00:07:55.675 --> 00:07:56.509
the possibility

00:07:56.509 --> 00:07:58.411
of fighter jets for Ukraine

00:07:58.411 --> 00:08:00.513
at their gathering in Hiroshima.

00:08:00.513 --> 00:08:01.614
Sources telling CNN

00:08:01.614 --> 00:08:02.882
that the Biden administration

00:08:02.882 --> 00:08:03.483
has signaled

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:04.584
to European allies

00:08:04.584 --> 00:08:05.718
that it would allow them

00:08:05.718 --> 00:08:09.422
to export U.s.-made F-16 jets to keep.

